Good morning Sysadmins,

My original question was:

I was wondering if anyone had managed to successfully compile and install
PGP on TRU64 v4.0G?

I was hoping to see my mailbox swamped with responses...  ;-)  Nonetheless,
my thanks goes to the following persons who responded: D. Stacks, J. Thomas
and M. Degerness.

M.D.: Has pgp 2.6.3ia running on 4.0F. No error reported.
-----------
J.T.: Used GNUPG v1.0.4.  An extract from his notes:

04/04/01,	Installed GNU Privacy Guard (GNUPG) 1.0.4.  
 		$ export CC="cc -std"
		$ gunzip gnupg-1.0.4.tar.gz
		$ tar -xvf gnupg-1.0.4.tar
            $ cd gnupg-1.0.4
		$ ./configure --enable-static-rnd=egd
		$ make
		$ make install

I think there was an error that could be ignored, if forget what program
didn't compile, but I didn't need it.

I had to install EGD v0.8 (Entropy Gathering Daemon)
------------------

Thanks to all and if I get successful results in my quest for the latest (as
possible) version of PGP on TRU64 v4.0G, I will send an update to the group.

Thanks again for your time and assistance,

Have a nice day,

   Serge Forget

Systems Operations


