Hi.  Do you have things logging to it from outside? 
If I remember
correctly, this once happened to us when we had a
printer attempting to
log to a 4.0G machine's syslog, and the printer did
not have a valid 
dns
reverse lookup for its host name.  The log entry did
not appear (making 
it
hard to track down) and syslog stopped logging
anything until it was
restarted.  The printer may not have complained
either.

Ann Cantelow

check the /var/adm/syslog file system full
check that the filesystem hasn't run out of inodes
(gazillions of 
teenie files)
check that log files are not excessively large
check EVM if you have it enabled (man page reference
to it)
if you haven't rebooted the system, try this as it may
clean up 
something hard to identify
---Pete Sherwood----

