Question was: disklabel -wr dskX in a cluster hangs.

short:
It "solved" itself.

long:
I received two suggestions. One did not work, one I did not
understand (I have no NT in my SAN). I gave up for the day.

During the night, both HSG80s crashed: Simultanous AdvFS panics
on all machines in the SAN. Oracle was not happy. After
everything has been recovered and running again, I found
that the "hung" disklabel -wr had written a correct disklabel
somehow.

Compaq looked through the logs but found nothing so far. The
only logged event is the "reset button pressed" to wake the
controllers up again.

