Original Question:

> Can anyone recommend an ATA 100/133 controller that is known to work in
> a Alpha pws 500au [not necessarily to run just Tru64 ie also FreeBSD]?

Answer:

	"There is no support in any version of Tru64 UNIX for ANY plug-in
	 ATA (aka IDE) controllers.  If you get lucky, you might manage to
	 find a card that will be totally ignored both by console firmware
	 (which has no support, as far as I know, on that system model, for
	 booting from an ATAPI or IDE drive connected to a plug-in card,
	 and if it already has an ATA controller chip on the motherboard
	 for a CDROM drive, it may not work right if you add a different
	 ATA controller chip), and by Tru64 UNIX.  Basically, you are on
	 uncharted waters -- not expected to work, but you might get lucky
	 if you try enough different combinations. "



